			"widgets_values":[
				"integrated_multimodal_description: A contemplative dance film aesthetic, featuring a ballet dancer in a sunlit studio, with volumetric god rays streaming through tall windows, soft cool-blue and warm-gold mixed lighting, pale muted color palette, shallow depth of field, and gentle 16mm film grain. The video opens on a wide shot of an empty ballet studio, wooden floors, tall windows with sheer white curtains, morning light filling the space.\n\n[Shot 1] The camera holds in a static wide shot as the dancer, wearing a pale lavender leotard with a flowing knee-length chiffon skirt, light pink tights, and soft ballet slippers, her dark hair in a tight neat bun, enters the frame from the left and walks slowly to the center of the studio, her posture upright and graceful, pausing to stand in first position, her arms resting gently at her sides.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.000, the camera cuts to a medium shot slowly pushing in with small amplitude at slow speed as the dancer begins a slow développé, lifting her right leg extended to the side with controlled precision, her arms rising in a graceful port de bras, her gaze following her hand, morning light catching the fine fabric of her skirt and the muscles in her leg, dust motes floating in the sunbeams.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:06.500, the camera cuts to a close-up low-angle shot as the dancer performs a slow pirouette, captured in slight slow motion, her chiffon skirt flaring outward in a soft circle, the bun at the back of her head visible, her expression focused and serene, the wooden floor reflecting her silhouette, the camera tilting up with small amplitude at slow speed following her movement.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:09.500, the camera cuts to a wide shot from behind as the dancer finishes her sequence and stands still in a final pose, one arm extended upward, the other out to the side, her body bathed in golden morning light from the windows, sheer curtains gently moving in a breeze, the studio quiet and still around her.\n\noverall_soundscape: The soft sound of ballet slippers on a wooden floor, the gentle rustle of chiffon fabric, distant birdsong from outside the windows, the faint whisper of a breeze through curtains, and a quiet room tone with subtle natural reverb of the empty studio.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A solo piano piece in the style of Erik Satie, slow and meditative, with simple, lingering notes and generous silence between phrases, gradually joined by a soft solo cello in the final shot, conveying dedication, quiet beauty, and the discipline of morning practice. \n",
				1344,
				768,
				73
			],
